        "The most important hyperparameters are:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Parameter | Meaning |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| `n_estimators` | Number of boosting rounds. |\n",
        "| `learning_rate` | Step size for each tree. |\n",
        "| `max_depth` | Depth of each tree. |\n",
        "| `subsample` | Fraction of observations used for each tree. |\n",
        "| `colsample_bytree` | Fraction of predictors used for each tree. |\n",
        "| `reg_lambda` | L2 regularization on leaf weights. |\n",
        "| `reg_alpha` | L1 regularization on leaf weights. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### Tuning XGBoost\n",
        "\n",
        "The hyperparameters work together.\n",
        "\n",
        "A common strategy is:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Start with shallow trees, such as `max_depth=2` or `max_depth=3`.\n",
        "2. Use a small learning rate, such as `0.03` or `0.05`.\n",
        "3. Use enough trees to let the model learn.\n",
        "4. Add subsampling to reduce overfitting.\n",
        "5. Tune regularization if the model still overfits.\n",
        "\n",
        "Example grid:"
